			"id": "agent-analysis-componentlibrary-detail-view-vm-orchestration",
			"interpretation": "componentlibrary exposes only three exports via Index.ets (ComponentHomeView, ComponentListModel, componentDetailConfig) and registers four NavDestination routes in router_map.json (ComponentListView, ComponentDetailView, CodePreviewView, PenKitView) bound to @Builder functions. Core responsibility is detail-page orchestration in ComponentDetailView: on assignViewData it reuses a ComponentDetailPageVM from the ComponentDetailManager singleton map keyed by componentName or creates one, assigns the NavPathStack, awaits InitComponentEvent(componentId), then drives INIT_DESCRIPTOR, INIT_RECOMMEND, WEB_CODE_EVENT in order via a displaySync frame pump (60–120Hz range), refreshing componentDetailState and clearing backPressed after each frame, stopping the pump on completion or rejection. onBackPressed swallows back by sending ChangeBackPressed(true)+BackPage when state.backPressed is false; onDisAppear releases displaySync; failures surface as VM loadingStatus (FAILED). Also wires breakpoint watch on GLOBAL_INFO, COLOR_MODE-driven status bar style, and a feedback sheet toolbar action. Maintenance contract: preserve singleton VM reuse, frame-ordered event sequence, back-press flag protocol, the three-export surface, and route-name/builder mappings.",
